    "contracts": [
      {
        "id": "physical_mux_ownership",
        "detail": "One source port per EXTI line0..15, shared by CPU and peripheral consumers. Mux outputs reach interconnect regardless of IMR/EMR. Masking CPU delivery does not quiesce DMA/ADC/DAC or other users. Reassignment requires all consumers stopped and common port/edge policy; no separate cloned line resources.",
        "evidence": [
          "RM0522:p446",
          "RM0522:p450"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "pending_masks",
        "detail": "Configurable hardware edges latch rising/falling pending only with IMR unmasked; event-only delivery does not latch EXTI flags (Table104). RPR/FPR are independent W1C bits, not edge counters. Pending interrupts prevent low-power entry per RM. Masking is not clearing existing pending state.",
        "evidence": [
          "RM0522:p449",
          "RM0522:p451",
          "RM0522:p454",
          "RM0522:p455"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "direct_event",
        "detail": "Direct lines have fixed rising wake-up and no EXTI pending/SWI. Peripheral interrupt reaches NVIC directly and is acknowledged in that peripheral. EXTI event may precede its peripheral status flag. Disabling EXTI masks does not establish that the peripheral NVIC source is disabled.",
        "evidence": [
          "RM0522:p445",
          "RM0522:p447",
          "RM0522:p449",
          "RM0522:p450"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "software_trigger",
        "detail": "SWIER write1 generates a rising event independently of edge settings; reads return0 and writing0 has no effect. It does not emulate a pad transition or prove downstream DMA/ADC routing. CPU mask behavior must follow the applicable source semantics; generic pending prose is retained separately.",
        "evidence": [
